# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: princ-without-argument-returns-nil -- (princ) should return the null symbol, so the REPL echo is blank
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: divergence
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-10-03

* Observed

#+begin_example
_$ (princ)
nil
_$ (type (princ))
nil
#+end_example

On AutoCAD and BricsCAD (princ) with no argument returns the NULL SYMBOL --
a symbol whose print name is empty: (type (princ)) is SYM and the console
echoes nothing. That is the reason every AutoLISP command function ends in
(princ): "exit quietly". clautolisp returns nil, so the REPL prints nil.

Found while implementing spec 5.6 rule 3 for the cadtui console (alref
Phase 4 S3): a CAD command line runs as (progn (command ...) (princ)) so
that, as at the vendors' prompt, nothing is echoed -- and clautolisp
echoes nil.

* To do

Make PRINC / PRIN1 / PRINT with no argument return the null symbol
(and check that the value printer prints it as nothing, that (null (princ))
is NIL, and that no test relies on nil). The spec's PRINC entry should say
so if it does not; verify against the vendor pages before changing it.
Probe-confirmable: (vl-symbol-name (princ)) -> "" on both vendors.

* Fixed per the spec (clautolisp 2.2.163, 2026-10-03)

The spec's PRINC entry already said "(princ) returns the *void* symbol
value"; clautolisp contradicted its own spec. PRINC / PRIN1 / PRINT with no
argument now return the empty-named symbol (AUTOLISP-VOID-SYMBOL): the REPL
echo is blank, (type (princ)) is SYM, (vl-symbol-name (princ)) is "", and
(null (princ)) is nil. (princ nil) now prints "nil" (the old WHEN that kept
the no-argument call silent also swallowed it).

The corpus asserted the old behaviour without provenance
(princ/prin1/print-no-arg-returns-nil): rewritten to the spec as
*-no-arg-returns-the-void-symbol. autolisp-test strict deviations 164 -> 162.

LEFT: probes/sources/probe-printer.lsp asks AutoCAD and BricsCAD directly
(type, symbol name, null-ness for all three); close when they answer -- the
CAD runners were asleep when this landed.

* Vendor answers -- closed (2026-10-04, clautolisp 2.2.172)

probes/sources/probe-printer.lsp, type / symbol name / null-ness / value:
  AutoCAD 2022 (job 16921381038): the void symbol from all three -- what
    2.2.163 implemented and the spec says.
  BricsCAD V26 (job 16921381039): (princ) and (print) return NIL, (prin1)
    the STRING "nil".
The BricsCAD dialects now follow BricsCAD (%NO-ARGUMENT-PRINTER-VALUE);
every other dialect keeps the void symbol. Checked on the built executable
(bricscad-v26 / bricscad-mac: (nil "nil" nil); autocad-2026: void symbols).
Corpus: tests/divergent/printer-no-argument.lsp pins each vendor.
